# enum variants; basanos incorrectly flags this as 'identical expressions'.
TESTING/tautological-test:crates/core/src/lib.rs

# =============================================================================
# ARCHITECTURE — glossary location
# =============================================================================

# WHY: Glossary lives at _llm/glossary.md per the llms.txt corpus standard.
# The root-level glossary.md location expected by this rule is not the
# canonical location for this repo (AI-corpus files go under _llm/).
ARCHITECTURE/no-glossary:Cargo.toml

# =============================================================================
# TOPOLOGY — shallow-struct for config structs (pre-existing design)
# =============================================================================

# WHY: EncodeOpts is intentionally a plain config struct; users build it with
# struct literal syntax. A smart constructor would add no value here.
TOPOLOGY/shallow-struct:crates/core/src/lib.rs

# =============================================================================
# TOPOLOGY — shallow-struct on data records owned by a sibling in the same file
# =============================================================================

# WHY: the rule reports "no in-file behavior" by looking for an inherent impl on
# the record itself. Each struct below is a plain data record whose behavior lives
# on the owning type declared in the same file — SwiGluMlp, QwenAttention,
# ModernBertLayer, StellaLayer, NameMap, Reader, RerankBatch, DecodeChain, Device.
# Splitting the record from its owner to satisfy the rule would move the fields
# away from the code that validates them.
#
# WHY: the weight structs additionally mirror a published checkpoint tensor layout
# (HF `[out, in]`), so their field set is upstream's, not a design choice of ours.
TOPOLOGY/shallow-struct:crates/transformers/src/mlp.rs
TOPOLOGY/shallow-struct:crates/transformers/src/attention.rs
TOPOLOGY/shallow-struct:crates/transformers/src/modernbert.rs
TOPOLOGY/shallow-struct:crates/encoders/src/modernbert.rs
TOPOLOGY/shallow-struct:crates/encoders/src/stella.rs
TOPOLOGY/shallow-struct:crates/loader/src/gguf.rs
TOPOLOGY/shallow-struct:crates/loader/src/mapping.rs
TOPOLOGY/shallow-struct:crates/rerank/src/batch.rs
TOPOLOGY/shallow-struct:crates/decode/src/chain.rs
TOPOLOGY/shallow-struct:crates/hipcore/src/device.rs

# WHY: ModernBertPreflight is the counter-example that shows the rule misfiring —
# it is already produced by a smart constructor (`ModernBertConfig::preflight()`)
# and is `#[non_exhaustive]`, which is precisely the remedy the rule proposes, and
# the rule still fires on it.
TOPOLOGY/shallow-struct:crates/rerank/src/config.rs

# =============================================================================
# RUST — field count fixed by an upstream schema
# =============================================================================

# WHY: ModernBertConfig is a serde DTO carrying `deny_unknown_fields`, deserialized
# from the published `Alibaba-NLP/gte-reranker-modernbert-base` config.json. Its 47
# fields are upstream's schema; dropping any of them makes the loader reject real
# checkpoints. The struct already carries an `#[expect(clippy::struct_excessive_bools)]`
# with the same justification.
RUST/struct-too-many-fields:crates/rerank/src/config.rs

# =============================================================================
# CI — attestation has no subject in this repo
# =============================================================================

# WARNING: revisit this the moment a publish or upload step is added. The
# exemption rests entirely on there being no artifact, not on attestation being
# unwanted.
#
# WHY: SLSA provenance and SBOM attestation attest a built artifact. This repo
# has three workflows — gate-attestation, release-please, security — and none
# builds, uploads, or publishes one: no `cargo publish`, no `upload-artifact`,
# no `gh release`. release-please.yml only runs the release-please action to
# open and maintain the release PR. Adding attest-build-provenance and
# attest-sbom here would emit attestations over nothing.
CI/release-yml-missing-attestation:.github/workflows/release-please.yml
